text:
Anna L.: Heads-up — opening a PR that reorders dark-mode semantic tokens to avoid the contrast cliffs we saw in the console charts. Can folks eyeball the proposed fallthrough order?
Kyle M.: Can you paste the token list here? Hard to grok from the pipeline diff.
Anna L.: Sure — quick excerpt: 
```
--surface-100: #0b0d0f;
--surface-200: #111215;
--surface-300: #17181a;
--surface-400: #1d1f22;
--surface-600: #2a2d30;
--accent-500: #6fb3ff;
--accent-400: #8cc6ff;
--code-bg: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
```
Mira S.: +1 on the ordering idea. Quick nit: code-bg at 0.03 reads a bit bright on long code blocks — it still creates a halo. Could we try a subtle inset overlay instead, like rgba(0,0,0,0.35) on top of surface-300? :thinking_face: 
Jonah R.: Also, chart series need better perceptual separation for >3 series. Suggest swapping series 2 to a teal and series 3 to a warm orange for the default ordering. For colorblind-safe defaults I usually start with #0072B2 (blue), #D55E00 (orange), #009E73 (green).
Sebastian: Accessibility nit — the 1px focus ring on primary buttons disappears against surface-200 when it's near the same luminance. Recommend 2px or switch to a high-contrast accent outline (maybe accent-400 with 0.9 alpha).
Kyle M.: Small implementation note: continuous smooth gradients in our chart lib spike the GPU paint for large datasets. Prefer stepped palettes or precomputed stops to keep GPU cost down.
Anna L.: Good catches. Action items: 1) Mira — tweak code-bg + run contrast checks; 2) Jonah — propose the alternate series palette and run colorblind sims; 3) Seb — pick final focus token delta and add to PR. I'll own merging after visual tests.
DesignBot: PR checklist update: visual regression snapshots queued, contrast report running, a11y smoke tests scheduled. Will post results. ✅
Mira S.: Uploading updated swatch PNG and the contrast matrix in ~10m. I tried code-bg: overlay rgba(0,0,0,0.28) and it removes the halo without killing token contrast.
Jonah R.: Ran quick colorblind sim — teal/orange/blue ordering maintains separability for Deutan/Protan. Pasting stops I used: #0072B2, #009E73, #D55E00, #CC79A7, #56B4E9.
Sebastian: Also suggest adding a short doc note about token fallthrough order — it helps platform teams when they override tokens in Dedicated/Private deployments.
Anna L.: That doc note is smart. One question: do we flip tokens v2 as the new default immediately or keep as opt-in for this release?
Kyle M.: Recommend opt-in for this cycle; flip default in the next release after the rollout. Less disruption for customers and gives us time to validate metrics (error rates, UX regressions).
Anna L.: Sounds good. Thanks everyone — I'll wait for the contrast report and then merge to the v2 branch. Will tag infra and charts owners before promoting to default. :tada:
